  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This CPO addresses the need for employers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; organizations in Kazakhstan to strengthen their institutional capacity, financial sustainability, and policy relevance, particularly in the area of occupational safety and health (OSH). The expected results include the consolidation of new, demand-driven services, increased revenue generation, and strengthened internal capacity to provide high-quality training and advisory services aligned with national priorities. ILO also supports employers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; organizations in building technical expertise and institutional structures that enhance their long-term sustainability.
Beneficiaries include employers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; organizations, their member enterprises, and the broader business community, particularly companies seeking practical solutions to OSH challenges. The strategy is implemented in cooperation with government institutions, workers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; organizations, and international partners, contributing to improved social dialogue, safer working environments, and more effective employer participation in policy discussions.</narrative>
  </description>
